// Kin's Sense: what someone holds closest, and whether they would ever give it.
// Played when Signe aims Sense at a person: knot sense_<id>.
// ALL TEXT IS A FIRST DRAFT by Claude, for Daniel to rewrite.

=== sense_hollow ===
A warm, breathing nothing. Like reaching into a coat and finding the pockets sewn shut.
-> END

=== sense_edda ===
Under the tiredness, one bright thing: a small girl looking up at an old man who looks back. She guards it like a coal.
She would give it to someone she trusted. Only to that.
-> END

=== sense_brita ===
A morning a hundred years ago: a man saying no, and then saying her name. She has carried it so long it has worn smooth.
She is tired of carrying it.
-> END

=== sense_gudmund ===
Stone. The feel of the first block he ever learned to read. The rest has gone dark around it.
He would give it, if he believed it would save the wall.
-> END

=== sense_clerk ===
A child's hand letting go of his sleeve, the first year. He keeps it like a debt.
He would pay it, to be rid of it.
-> END

=== sense_arn ===
Fear, and under it a girl's voice saying there is a sky under the ice.
He would give you anything. He is nine.
-> END

=== sense_knut ===
His children asleep in the lower quarter, and all that water above them.
He would give nothing. Everything he has is spoken for.
-> END

=== sense_ebbe ===
His wife, laughing on the jetty. It is the only warm thing left in him.
-> END

=== sense_hermit ===
The lake, every crack of it, laid out like a map.
-> END

=== sense_gerda ===
A grandmother's voice, telling it right.
-> END

=== sense_olle ===
Columns of names. Under them, a guilt he never looks at.
-> END

=== sense_lilja ===
You. Mostly you.
-> END

=== sense_torvald ===
Two girls on the ice, and a woman he does not let himself think about.
-> END
